
To compile a .exe a wine environment is needed with
gcc-15 at the least and gnu prolog version 1.5.0 installed on it
once installed, grab the SDL2 libraries from

https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_ttf/releases#release-release-2.24.0

and related sites. Versions need to be 
SDL2-2.32
SDL2_ttf-2.24
...
...
...

make sure they are placed inside /usr/local/x86_64-w64-mingw32/bin
this is done automatically with `make cross` when unpacking and installing
the mingw64 packages


then run make and it should compile

------------------------------------------

To run properly with hardware acceleration under wine

What made it work is the following:
	setting x11 to be the graphics driver
	setting renderer to gl
	disable DLL overrides
	sound set to pulseaudio (although sound was working fine before)
